      "text": "First, we complete the square on both sides of the equation $x^2 + y^2 = 10x - 6y - 34$. The left side becomes $(x^2 - 10x) + y^2 = (x - 5)^2 - 25 + y^2$, and the right side becomes $10x - 6y - 34 = 10(x - 5 - y) - 34 = (x - 7)(2(x - 7) - 1) = 2(x + 8)(8 - x)$. Thus, we have $(x - 5)^2 + y^2 = 2(x + 8)(8 - x)$. Since the sum of the squares of two numbers is equal to their product, their product must also equal 0, so $(x - 5)^2 = 0$ and $2(x + 8)(8 - x) = 0$. Solving these equations gives $x = 5$, $x = -8$, or $x = 3$.\n\nIf $x = 5$, then $y = x - 8 = -3$, so $x + y = 2$.\nIf $x = -8$, then $y = -3$, so $x + y = -11$.\nIf $x = 3$, then $y = -5$, so $x + y = -8$.",
